 "$comment": [
  "lib/office-fonts/powerpoint-script-fallbacks.json: the face PowerPoint for Windows draws a character in when a",
  "run's Office face, which Windows has, lacks it -- Calibri for a sans face, Cambria for a serif one -- for every",
  "Office face with a metric clone (lib/office-fonts/metric-clones/metrics: its character map is the Office face's).",
  "",
  "The rule is read from PowerPoint for Windows' own PDF (MRAI-corpus/office-truth/probes/tp-fallback, 11-18:",
  "Cyrillic, Greek and Vietnamese in 26 installed faces, character by character, whatever the run's language):",
  "the face's OS/2 panose serif style 11-15 (sans) -> Calibri (Tw Cen MT, Gill Sans MT, Century Gothic, Franklin",
  "Gothic Book, Lucida Sans Unicode, Trebuchet MS, Arial Narrow), 2-10 -> Cambria (Rockwell, Garamond, Georgia,",
  "Book Antiqua). The panose is read from the Office face file the metric record names, found by its digest"
 ],
